<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Avatar</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A compact visual representation of a user, showing a Gravatar image, initials, or a
    fallback icon.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <Avatar name="Nicolas Bettenburg" email="nicbet@kuy.io"/>
      <Avatar name="Jane Doe" initials="JD"/>
      <Avatar name="Unknown User"/>
    </div>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Avatar name=\"Jane Doe\" initials=\"JD\"/>\n\n<Avatar name=\"Jane Doe\" email=\"jane@example.com\"/>\n\n<Avatar name=\"Unknown\"/>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      Avatar resolves its display in order of specificity: if an <code>email</code> is provided,
      it attempts to load a Gravatar image. If that fails (or no email is given), it falls back
      to <code>initials</code>. If neither email nor initials are provided, a generic user icon
      is shown.
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-muted/50 overflow-hidden mt-4">
    <CodeBlock code={"Avatar display priority:\n1. Gravatar (from email) → fallback on load error\n2. Initials (first two characters, uppercased)\n3. Icon (default: user, overridable via icon prop)"}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Use Avatar wherever you reference a user: comment threads, team lists, navigation bars,
      profile cards, and activity feeds. The component provides a consistent visual anchor that
      helps users scan lists of people quickly.
    </p>
    <p>
      For generic images that aren't user avatars (product photos, thumbnails), use the
      <a href="/components/image">Image</a> component instead.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      When an <code>email</code> is provided, the component generates a Gravatar URL using an MD5
      hash of the email address. The image loads lazily and if the Gravatar service returns a 404
      (no avatar registered), the component falls back to initials or the user icon automatically
      via an <code>onerror</code> handler.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <code>name</code> prop sets both the <code>title</code> attribute (shown on hover) and
      <code>aria-label</code> for screen reader accessibility.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Sizes</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Five sizes from <strong>xs</strong> (24px) to <strong>xl</strong> (64px). Use
        <strong>sm</strong> in compact lists, <strong>md</strong> as the default, and
        <strong>lg</strong>/<strong>xl</strong> for profile headers.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex items-end gap-4">
        <Avatar name="User" initials="XS" size="xs"/>
        <Avatar name="User" initials="SM" size="sm"/>
        <Avatar name="User" initials="MD" size="md"/>
        <Avatar name="User" initials="LG" size="lg"/>
        <Avatar name="User" initials="XL" size="xl"/>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Shape</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Avatars are round by default. Set <code>square</code> for a rounded-rectangle shape,
        useful for team or organisation logos.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <Avatar name="Round" initials="RD" size="lg"/>
        <Avatar name="Square" initials="SQ" size="lg" square/>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Custom Icon</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Override the default user icon with the <code>icon</code> prop. Accepts a string
        name or a hash for variant control. Useful for bots, service accounts, or role indicators.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <Avatar name="Admin" icon="shield-halved" size="lg"/>
        <Avatar name="Bot" icon="robot" size="lg"/>
        <Avatar name="Support" icon="headset" size="lg"/>
        <Avatar name="GitHub" icon={{name: "github", variant: "brands"}} size="lg" square/>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Fallback Chain</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>The three states: Gravatar image (from email), initials text, and the default user icon.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <Avatar name="Nicolas Bettenburg" email="nicbet@kuy.io" size="lg"/>
        <Avatar name="Jane Doe" initials="JD" size="lg" email="doesnotexist@example.com"/>
        <Avatar name="Unknown User" size="lg"/>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">In Context</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Avatars pair naturally with text for user references in lists, comments, and cards.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 w-full">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Avatar name="Alice" initials="AL"/>
          <div>
            <Heading size="sm" as="div">Alice</Heading>
            <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="div">Just merged a pull request</Text>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Avatar name="Bob" initials="BO"/>
          <div>
            <Heading size="sm" as="div">Bob</Heading>
            <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="div">Left a comment on the design doc</Text>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    '} align="start"/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Always provide a <code>name</code> for accessibility.</li>
          <li>Use consistent sizes within the same list or context.</li>
          <li>Prefer email-based Gravatars when available for real user photos.</li>
          <li>Use initials when you have the user's name but no email.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Avatar for non-user images — use Image instead.</li>
          <li>Show more than two initials — they won't fit at small sizes.</li>
          <li>Omit the <code>name</code> prop — the avatar becomes inaccessible.</li>
          <li>Mix round and square avatars in the same list.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">name</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any text</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">email</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Email address (for Gravatar)</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">initials</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">1–2 characters</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">icon</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String / Hash</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Icon name or {name:, variant:}</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">"user"</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">size</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Symbol</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">xs, sm, md, lg, xl</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">md</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">round</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">square</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
